  "title": "Coast Guard rescues 3 from boats stuck in ice near Hole in the Wall Glacier",
  "description": "A Coast Guard Air Station Sitka MH-60 Jayhawk helicopter aircrew hoists three jet boaters from their boats, that were stuck in about one foot of ice, approximately five miles northeast of Hole in the Wall Glacier on the Taku River, Alaska, Oct. 25, 2020. The operator of good Samaritan vessel Nantucket initially reported two of the vessels stuck in ice, and a call from a spouse of one of the boaters reported the party overdue. (U.S. Coast Guard video by Air Station Sitka)",
